H: Researchers find consistent 'pro-girl' gap in 10 A level subjects
T: Grading bias
C: UK
D: 2026
O: University of Cambridge
B: An analysis of 351k students finds that, girls were 3-11% more likely to have their grades overpredicted and 15-41% less likely to have ther grades underpredicted than boys. This holds true even after controlling for socioeconomic group, ethincity,class size, school attended. Teachers maybe picking up on motivation and classroom engagement and thereby creating a halo effect.
U: https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0272775726000567
